/* IfcSheet test fixture for the structural grid (issue 47). Generated by a throw-away script, then read by hand.
   Units: MILLIMETRE, so a missing unit scale shows as a factor of 1000.
   Grid: axes A (x = 0), B (x = 6000) running along y, 1 (y = 0), 2 (y = 5000) running along x, in the grid's own frame.
   The grid's ObjectPlacement is relative to the IfcBuilding: translated (10000, 20000), rotated 15 degrees about Z.
   Columns A1 B1 A2 B2 (400 x 400, 3000 high) and four walls on the grid lines hang under the storey, placed in that
   same frame by their world positions: (10000,20000) + R(15deg) * (0|6000, 0|5000). Each axis passes through the
   centres of two columns. FZK-Haus has no IfcGrid, hence this file. */
